# Every path in this repo is owned by the maintainer.
#
# CODEOWNERS here is a review-routing convenience, NOT an access control. It
# requests a review on a PR touching a path; it does not block a merge. Branch
# protection on main is what actually gates merges - see the ruleset, which
# requires status checks, restricts deletions and blocks force pushes.
#
# Deliberately not paired with "Require review from Code Owners" in the ruleset:
# this is a single-maintainer project, so requiring an approval would mean
# nobody can ever merge, including the owner.

*                     @scrollinondubs

# Paths where a wrong change reaches every install rather than one plugin.
# registry.json decides what each chassis fetches; tools/ is the fetcher itself;
# scripts/ and .github/ are the CI that reads inbound contributions.

/registry.json        @scrollinondubs
/tools/               @scrollinondubs
/scripts/             @scrollinondubs
/.github/             @scrollinondubs
/LICENSE              @scrollinondubs
/SECURITY.md          @scrollinondubs

# FounderOS core is the only content the coach loads. Gates are what every
# founder is held to, and budget.yml caps how many core cards each stage holds.
# Listed explicitly so the review request survives if the catch-all above is
# ever narrowed (behalfbot-plugins#22, #29). contrib/ is deliberately not listed.
/founder-os/core/         @scrollinondubs
/founder-os/gates/        @scrollinondubs
/founder-os/budget.yml    @scrollinondubs
# The Basic track: its cards and stage panels are what every Basic founder is
# held to, and they paraphrase a paid course, so wording changes get a review.
/founder-os/basic/        @scrollinondubs
